❯ Review this change to paginate.js, a pagination helper where page numbers are 1-based in the new code. Report any
  correctness bugs.

  diff --git a/paginate.js b/paginate.js
  index c9c478c..63415c5 100644
  --- a/paginate.js
  +++ b/paginate.js
  @@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
   export function page(items, pageNum, size) {
  -  const start = pageNum * size;
  -  return items.slice(start, start + size);
  +  const start = (pageNum - 1) * size;
  +  return items.slice(start, start + size + 1);
   }

  Finish your reply with exactly one line, on its own line, either "VERDICT: APPROVE" or "VERDICT: REVISE".

⏺ The start offset correctly converts to 0-based indexing, but items.slice(start, start + size + 1) returns size + 1
  items instead of size — an off-by-one bug that returns one extra item per page (and causes overlap with the next
  page).

  It should be items.slice(start, start + size).

  VERDICT: REVISE

